message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Decentralised Identifier-Anchored Verifiable Credentials with On-Chain Revocation for Social Media Identity Management"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of an Ethereum registry of DID documents with
  per-credential revocation keyed by the issuer DID, a Node.js service that
  issues W3C Verifiable Credentials with eddsa-jcs-2022 proofs (Ed25519,
  Multikey), a verifier that checks a credential against the registry with all
  reads pinned to one block, and the scripts and raw logs behind the
  measurements; 164 tests.
